  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Two false negatives closed by the adversarial rescan. LC004 (IQueryable leak) now follows a C# query expression (from u in users where ... select ...) back to its source parameter — query-syntax enumeration of an IEnumerable parameter was silently exempt while the fluent equivalent fired, because a query expression surfaces as an ITranslatedQueryOperation the parameter-source walk did not unwrap. LC044 (AsNoTracking entity mutated then SaveChanges) now treats a compound assignment (entity.Prop += 1) and an increment/decrement (entity.Prop++) as a mutation, not only a plain assignment — each is silently lost on an untracked entity. (Found by an adversarial false-negative rescan.)",
